---
import TopNav from '../components/TopNav.astro';
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<title>The timeline — Six Years Out</title>
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,400;9..144,600&family=Inter:wght@400;500&display=swap">
</head>
<body>
<TopNav current="timeline" />
<div class="wrap">

<header class="intro">
  <p class="lede">This page reads bottom to top — 6th grade at the bottom, college at the top. Scroll down to find your grade or jump straight to the start.</p>
  <a class="jump" href="#start">Start at the beginning ↓</a>
</header>

<div class="line">
<div class="spine" id="spine"></div>

<div class="row">
  <div></div>
  <div class="rail">
    <div class="dot" id="top-dot" style="background:var(--g12)">
      <svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M12 4 2 9l10 5 10-5-10-5Z"/><path d="M6 11.5V16c0 1.6 2.7 3 6 3s6-1.4 6-3v-4.5"/>
        <path d="M20.6 8.4v5.2"/><circle cx="20.6" cy="14.8" r="1.2" fill="#fff" stroke="none"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="block">
    <h2>College</h2>
    <p class="say">This is what everything below is building toward.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row">
  <div class="block right">
    <h2>You submit your applications</h2>
    <p class="say">Senior year still counts.</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g12)">What to do now</h3>
    <p>Write the essays over the summer, before school starts</p>
    <p>Finalize your recommendation letters</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g12)">What most people get wrong</h3>
    <p>Writing the essays in October instead. They're the only part of the application you fully control, so don't procrastinate</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g12)">What counts</h3>
    <p>Senior grades still count. Colleges can withdraw an offer if they drop a lot</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g12)">Tests and deadlines</h3>
    <p>You can retake the SAT or ACT in the fall if you'd like</p>
    <p>Financial aid forms open in the fall</p>
    <p>Deadlines vary by school. Some offer earlier options, like early decision or early action</p>
    <a class="more" href="/grades/12">How to: 12th grade →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="rail"><div class="dot" style="background:var(--g12);color:#fff">12</div></div>
  <div></div>
</div>

<div class="row">
  <div></div>
  <div class="rail"><div class="dot" style="background:var(--g11);color:#fff">11</div></div>
  <div class="block">
    <h2>The year that matters the most</h2>
    <p class="say">Tests, hardest classes, and the teachers who write about you.</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g11)">What to do now</h3>
    <p>Most schools accept either the SAT or the ACT. Picking one early can help you focus your prep, though it's fine to try both if you're not sure which fits you</p>
    <p>Ask for recommendation letters in the spring. By fall of senior year, teachers will be drowning in other students' requests for them</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g11)">What most people get wrong</h3>
    <p>Taking on more hard classes than you can actually handle well. An overloaded schedule doesn't help anyone</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g11)">What counts</h3>
    <p>Junior grades weigh more than any other year</p>
    <p>How rigorous your classes are matters too, not just your grades</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g11)">Tests and deadlines</h3>
    <p>The October PSAT is the one that qualifies for National Merit</p>
    <p>SAT or ACT in spring, AP exams in May</p>
    <a class="more" href="/grades/11">How to: 11th grade →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row">
  <div class="block right">
    <h2>Go deeper, not wider</h2>
    <p class="say">Continue on with one extracurricular that you're committed to, rather than adding more.</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What to do now</h3>
    <p>Take a free practice SAT and ACT to see which one suits you</p>
    <p>Try and take a leadership role in your main activity</p>
    <p>Consider entering a competition in your field</p>
    <p>Do a summer program or internship</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What most people get wrong</h3>
    <p>Worrying about a PSAT score that doesn't count, while skipping the practice tests that would actually tell you something</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What counts</h3>
    <p>First real leadership in something you've already done a year</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">Tests and deadlines</h3>
    <p>PSAT 10 in the spring, AP exams in May</p>
    <a class="more" href="/grades/10">How to: 10th grade →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="rail"><div class="dot" style="background:var(--g10);color:#fff">10</div></div>
  <div></div>
</div>

<div class="row">
  <div></div>
  <div class="rail"><div class="dot" style="background:var(--g9);color:var(--g12)">9</div></div>
  <div class="block">
    <h2>Your transcript starts</h2>
    <p class="say">The first year colleges will actually see.</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What to do now</h3>
    <p>Pick one or two things you'd still want to be doing as a senior</p>
    <p>Start a passion project</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What most people get wrong</h3>
    <p>Joining eight clubs and exploring their options, rather than centering on one or two passion-driven extracurriculars. Four years of one or two passion-driven extracurriculars is worth more than one year of eight</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What counts</h3>
    <p>Every grade from here is part of your GPA</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">Tests and deadlines</h3>
    <p>Some schools give the PSAT 8/9. It's just for practice. Colleges never see the score</p>
    <a class="more" href="/grades/9">How to: 9th grade →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row">
  <div class="block right">
    <h2>Gearing up for high school</h2>
    <p class="say">Math matters. So does choosing your high school classes appropriately.</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What to do now</h3>
    <p>Take Algebra I if you can. This makes calculus reachable in high school</p>
    <p>Read for fun constantly, which is the best long-run test prep there is</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What most people get wrong</h3>
    <p>Picking high school classes without realizing it's a four-year commitment. The classes you choose as a freshman can lock you out of classes later on, like calculus, as a sophomore, junior, or senior</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What counts</h3>
    <p>Algebra I shows on your transcript. Nothing else from this year does</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">Tests and deadlines</h3>
    <p>State testing in some districts, but none that count towards a college application</p>
    <a class="more" href="/grades/8">How to: 8th grade →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="rail"><div class="dot" style="background:var(--g8);color:var(--g12)">8</div></div>
  <div></div>
</div>

<div class="row">
  <div></div>
  <div class="rail"><div class="dot" style="background:var(--g7);color:var(--g12)">7</div></div>
  <div class="block">
    <h2>Find out what you like</h2>
    <p class="say">Don't be afraid to explore both inside and outside of the classroom.</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What to do now</h3>
    <p>Join clubs you're curious about, quit the ones you don't like</p>
    <p>Try one thing that seems slightly too hard</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What most people get wrong</h3>
    <p>Waiting until 9th grade to start exploring clubs and extracurriculars, when 7th grade is actually a better time to start. Not thinking too much about college itself in 7th grade is still the right move</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What counts</h3>
    <p>Nothing. This year is free to experiment</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">Tests and deadlines</h3>
    <p>State testing in some districts, but none that count towards a college application</p>
    <a class="more" href="/grades/7">How to: 7th grade →</a>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row" id="start">
  <div class="block right">
    <h2>Only one decision matters</h2>
    <p class="say">If math interests you, find out if your school has an accelerated math program.</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What to do now</h3>
    <p>If you like math, find out whether your school has an accelerated track and how you get on it</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What most people get wrong</h3>
    <p>Not realizing math placement is a decision at all. It's usually made on 5th and 6th grade scores, and it's what decides whether Algebra I in 8th grade is even available to you</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">What counts</h3>
    <p>Nothing goes on your college application. But this one placement shapes the next six years of math</p>
    <h3 style="color:var(--g10)">Tests and deadlines</h3>
    <p>Whatever placement test your district uses, if it uses one</p>
    <p>State testing in some districts, but none that count towards a college application</p>
    <a class="more" href="/grades/6">How to: 6th grade →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="rail"><div class="dot pale" id="bot-dot" style="background:var(--g6);color:var(--g12)">6</div></div>
  <div></div>
</div>

<div class="key">
  <div class="chip on">Grades 6, 7 and 8<b>explore</b></div>
  <div class="chip">Grades 9 and 10<b>build</b></div>
  <div class="chip">Grades 11 and 12<b>apply</b></div>
</div>

<div class="foot">
  <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#185FA5" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M12 19V5"/><path d="m5 12 7-7 7 7"/>
  </svg>
  <p class="up">Start here and scroll up</p>
  <p class="sub">You're already somewhere on this line.</p>
</div>

</div>
</div>

<style>
:root{
  --paper:#FAF4EA;
  --ink:#12283D;
  --ink-soft:#4A5C70;
  --ink-faint:#7A8899;
  --rule:#E4D9C6;
  --g6:#E6F1FB;
  --g7:#B5D4F4;
  --g8:#85B7EB;
  --g9:#378ADD;
  --g10:#185FA5;
  --g11:#0C447C;
  --g12:#042C53;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{
  margin:0;
  background:var(--paper);
  color:var(--ink);
  font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;
  font-size:16px;
  line-height:1.6;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}
.wrap{max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 24px 40px}

.intro{text-align:center;max-width:480px;margin:32px auto 56px}
.intro .lede{font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0 0 20px}
.jump{
  display:inline-block;font-size:14px;padding:10px 18px;border-radius:8px;
  border:1px solid var(--g10);color:var(--g10);text-decoration:none;background:transparent;
}
.jump:hover{background:#fff}
.jump:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:2px}

.line{position:relative}
.spine{
  position:absolute;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:14px;border-radius:7px;z-index:0;
  background:linear-gradient(to bottom,var(--g12),var(--g11),var(--g10),var(--g9),var(--g8),var(--g7),var(--g6));
}
.row{
  display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 100px minmax(0,1fr);
  align-items:start;position:relative;z-index:1;
}
.rail{display:flex;justify-content:center}
.dot{
  width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-size:27px;font-weight:600;
}
.dot.pale{border:1px solid var(--g9)}
.block{padding-bottom:52px}
.block.right{text-align:right}
.block h2{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;margin:6px 0 4px}
.block .say{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0 0 16px}
.block h3{font-size:15px;font-weight:500;margin:16px 0 4px}
.block p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0 0 4px}
.more{
  display:inline-block;margin-top:18px;font-size:13px;text-decoration:none;
  padding:7px 14px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #C9B99E;color:var(--ink);
}
.more:hover{background:#fff}
.more:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:2px}

.key{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding-top:12px;position:relative;z-index:1}
.chip{
  padding:8px 15px;border-radius:20px;font-size:13px;
  background:#fff;color:var(--ink-faint);border:1px solid var(--rule);
}
.chip b{display:block;font-weight:500;font-size:11px;margin-top:1px}
.chip.on{background:var(--g6);color:var(--g11);border-color:var(--g7)}

.foot{text-align:center;padding-top:22px;position:relative;z-index:1}
.foot .up{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-size:17px;margin:6px 0 0}
.foot .sub{font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:2px 0 0}

@media (max-width:640px){
  .wrap{padding:20px 16px 32px}
  .row{grid-template-columns:64px minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px}
  .spine{left:32px}
  .rail{justify-content:flex-start}
  .block.right{text-align:left}
  .row .rail{order:1}
  .row .block{order:2}
  .row > .block:first-child{order:2}
  .row > div:empty{display:none}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  *{transition:none!important;animation:none!important}
}
</style>

<script>
(function(){
  var line=document.querySelector('.line'),
      spine=document.getElementById('spine'),
      top=document.getElementById('top-dot'),
      bot=document.getElementById('bot-dot');
  function place(){
    if(!line||!spine||!top||!bot)return;
    var l=line.getBoundingClientRect(),t=top.getBoundingClientRect(),b=bot.getBoundingClientRect();
    spine.style.top=Math.round(t.top-l.top+t.height/2)+'px';
    spine.style.bottom=Math.round(l.bottom-b.bottom+b.height/2)+'px';
  }
  place();
  window.addEventListener('resize',place);
  if(document.fonts&&document.fonts.ready){document.fonts.ready.then(place);}
  setTimeout(place,400);
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
